                <pb facs="0607" n="517" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg517"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 8 in No. 82.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram taken from the London Times of March 8,
                        1875.]</seg></opener>
                <p>The Pope has permitted the Austrian bishops to comply with the law compelling
                    them to mention to the authorities the names of priests appointed to livings. As
                    the refusal of the Prussian bishops to obey the analogous law recently enacted
                    in this country is the principal cause of the ecclesiastical war with Prussia,
                    the concession made to Austria is regarded by the German press as another proof
                    that the Pope is actuated, not by religious, but by political motives in
                    resisting the statutes of Prussia and Germany.</p>
            </div>
